module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.instrument_unobservable_as_its_subject_grows

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data instrument_unobservable_as_its_subject_grows: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "instrument_unobservable_as_its_subject_grows" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "**an instrument becomes unobservable as its subject grows** (INVALID STATE: a measurement's only write is a rendering whose SIZE IS PROPORTIONAL TO THE POPULATION IT REPORTS, on a channel with a size limit. The instrument is therefore LEAST readable exactly when its subject is largest, which is when it is worth reading. ",

    "This is not a logging defect and must not be filed as one: it is the same shape as a check that greens by construction, one layer out -- an instrument that reports faithfully on every small subject and silently stops reporting on the only subjects that would have changed a decision. ",

    "WHY NOBODY CATCHES IT: every small run reports fine, so the instrument accumulates a history of working, and the failure begins precisely where no one has a baseline to compare against. ",

    "**SPECIMEN, 2026-09-05/06 (jolly-badger-374), MEASURED ON A REQUIRED RUN RATHER THAN A FIXTURE.** `v1.compiler.claim_executor`'s required-ci block emits a module census with `eprintln!` and `{:?}` over identity vectors. On run 33990451798 the BUILD lane's `judged-module-identities` line is 44,727 bytes and SURVIVED intact -- it closes its bracket at 1224 identities, and the next largest line in that job is 790 bytes. The capture then STOPS. The FLOOR lane (`lane=witnesses`) shows no census line at all: its last captured line is the `phases_run` announcement, the `eprintln!` immediately before the census. ",

    "So the threshold is BRACKETED rather than named: above 44,727 bytes and at or below the floor lane's own judged line. The line that never appears in the build job is `admitted-module-identities`, roughly three and a half times the surviving one. ",

    "**TWO MECHANISMS PROPOSED AND BOTH REFUTED BY MEASUREMENT, recorded because a finding that rules out its own alternatives is worth more than one that asserts a cause.** PER-LINE DROP is refuted: neither job SKIPS the oversized line and continues -- both stop at the census position and nothing follows. CUMULATIVE OUTPUT CAP is refuted: the floor job captured 781,698 bytes in 3,727 lines against the build's 160,305 in 917, so a global cap would have cut the floor long before, and the two jobs stop at the same PLACE rather than the same SIZE. ",

    "**THE CONTROL THAT LOCATES IT, same run and same runner, discriminated by which binary executes.** `heal-generated-artifacts` (146,093 bytes) and `witnesses` (5,009 bytes) BOTH end with the ordinary `Cleaning up orphan processes` completion line. The two `claim_executor` lanes emit no completion line at all. So it is not only the census that is lost: THE REMAINDER OF THE STEP'S CAPTURED OUTPUT GOES WITH IT. ",

    "**A THIRD HYPOTHESIS WAS NAMED AND REFUTED, AND IT IS THE ONE THAT WOULD HAVE MADE THIS A CORRECTNESS DEFECT** -- the process dying while formatting a multi-hundred-kilobyte string, with the step still reporting success. In `claim_executor` the order is census, then the `FAILED PHASE` loop, then the measurement-receipt write; and THAT RECEIPT EXISTS AS A PUBLISHED ARTIFACT FOR THE SAME RUN, standing `measurement_completed`. A process killed while formatting could not have written it. The process ran past the census, past the failure loop, and wrote its receipt. ",

    "**SEVERITY, STATED DOWN RATHER THAN UP.** Losing the `FAILED PHASE` lines DOES NOT LOSE THE FAILURE: the lane's verdict rides the exit code and the check conclusion, not the log. A failing phase still fails the job with its log gone. WHAT IS DESTROYED IS THE DIAGNOSIS, NOT THE REFUSAL -- a red that cannot be READ, never a red that reads GREEN. This row explicitly forecloses the stronger reading. ",

    "**ON THE NUMBERS ABOVE, BECAUSE SECTION 6 SAYS NAME THE INSTRUMENT AND NEVER TRANSCRIBE ITS OUTPUT, AND THIS ROW IS THE ONE CASE THAT CANNOT.** They are DATED READINGS OF ONE IMMUTABLE RUN, not a live census: run 33990451798 is fixed, so unlike a reference count they cannot drift as the corpus changes, and the emitting producer is named by symbol rather than by position -- `v1.compiler.claim_executor`, the required-ci block, whose census statements are unconditional and not lane-gated. That is the form the two neighbouring rows in this same roster already use for run-scoped specimens. WHAT MAKES THIS ROW DIFFERENT IS THE POINT OF IT, AND THE CLAIM IS DELIBERATELY NARROW RATHER THAN FLAT: it is NOT that nothing here can be re-derived. THESE readings belong to ONE RUN whose captured output cannot be regenerated identically; THE CLASS stays perfectly re-derivable by a new run, which will lose its own census the same way. Section 6 states the test that decides which of the two a number is -- if a measurement is worth re-deriving it is worth an entry point, and if it is not worth an entry point it is not an instrument but a ONE-OFF -- and the rule exists so a transcribed number cannot ROT AWAY FROM A PRODUCER THAT WOULD HAVE KEPT IT CURRENT. A dated observation of one immutable run has no such producer to rot away from: re-running yields a different run, not a corrected reading of this one. So the entry point this row owes is for the CLASS and is named below, while the readings are carried as a dated one-off with their run, their bracket and their retention limit attached. Re-running the lane does not reproduce them -- it produces a new run whose census is lost the same way -- and the captured log that carried the surviving fragment is retained by the forge for a bounded window, after which the evidence for this row is gone while the defect remains. So the numbers are stated with their run, their bracket and their limit, and the entry point offered for RE-DERIVING THE CLASS rather than the readings is the discriminator named below: emit the census to a file and a one-line summary to stdout, then observe whether the completion lines return. A row about an unreadable instrument that cited a re-derivable instrument for its own evidence would be claiming the very readability it exists to deny. ",

    "**RUNG FOUND AT: mitigatable.** The verdict is intact and the census is recomputed on every run, so nothing is silently wrong; what is lost is the ability to read it. ",

    "**CEILING: structurally impossible for this class of write, and the construction ALREADY EXISTS IN THE SAME BINARY.** A measurement whose destination is a published artifact rather than a size-limited rendering cannot become unreadable by growing. The census does not need a new mechanism invented for it: the measurement-receipt path already works, is written by the same process a few statements later, and survived the very run whose census did not. ",

    "**NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, NAMED AS A CAPABILITY:** every required-lane census emitted to the receipt/artifact route that its own measurement receipt already travels, with any stdout rendering reduced to a bounded summary that names the artifact, sufficient that a census's readability is INDEPENDENT OF ITS POPULATION SIZE. A larger corpus must not be able to make a required lane's own measurement disappear. ",

    "**WHAT IS NOT CLAIMED, and the boundary is deliberate.** WHERE the loss occurs -- inside `claim_executor`, inside the runner's log uploader, or in the stream between them -- is UNDETERMINED. The capture cannot distinguish them, and naming one would be a fabricated mechanism attached to a real measurement. The cheap discriminator, unrun: emit the census to a file and a one-line summary to stdout, then check whether the completion lines return, capturing the process exit code alongside. ",

    "**BOUNDARY AGAINST `empty_observation_narrow` and `selection_view_read_as_population`:** there the instrument reports about a narrowed subject and a reader over-reads it. Here the instrument's subject is correct and complete, and its REPORT does not arrive at all -- the reader has nothing to over-read. The two compound where a census that would have exposed a narrowing is itself the line that vanishes.)",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
